            <ArticleTitle>Is 'sinus' pain really sinusitis?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>558-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.12968/hmed.2014.75.10.558</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>So-called 'sinus pain' is a common complaint in GP and ear, nose and throat clinics, and patients often receive treatment with antibiotics and decongestants. Recent evidence suggests that facial pain may not be related to the sinuses at all and that doctors may have to rethink their prescribing strategy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
